<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1620corr-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 16 to 20 corrections"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.1.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1620corr-lineage/1.1.0> ;
    owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1620corr-lineage/1.0.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1620corr_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.1.0 (2026-11-26): Scope stage only (one stage per version): the scope statement with its areas, deliverables and exclusions, derived from the Mission stage's verified gaps (Lineage Operating Discipline v163.0.7, 3d). The shape rules that the Lineage12 scope stage found only on a second pass are answered here at once (each area has a location, a counted measure and a layer; each deliverable a layer and a quoted mission clause; each exclusion a concern, a layer and a decision-maker). The four gaps named NOT MEASURED in 1.0.0 are scope items here (page test on the current pipeline, matching code, links and pictures, story repeat) and are measured before any goal rests on them. Lesson taken from the Lineage12 closure: an exclusion names the act it forbids exactly (modifying or deleting an existing file), so that the planned new own-version files do not read as a breach, and the folders allowed to change are listed in the scope text."""@en .

ex:Area13_Conversion a backlog:ScopeArea ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage13 ;
    rdfs:label "Specs for the generic deck builder (chapters 18 to 20)"@en ;
    backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ;
    backlog:areaLocation "08-tooling/ch18-deck/ (spec_v3_0_0 exists), ch19-deck/ (no spec folder, per-chapter builder deck_build_v1_0_0.py), ch20-deck/ (spec_v2_0_1 exists); a new spec folder per chapter beside them" ;
    backlog:areaMeasure "3 chapters; 2 spec folders exist (chapters 18 and 20) and are older than the rulings; 1 chapter (19) has none; chapters 16 and 17 already have spec_v4_0_0 and are not re-specified" .
